00:12:58.483 --> 00:13:01.573
From youtube Yumna says,
can you help me resolve

00:13:01.573 --> 00:13:04.773
one of my problems, my
eldest son does not take

00:13:04.773 --> 00:13:07.966
his studies seriously, he avoids studying.

00:13:08.843 --> 00:13:11.823
I think this is a central
problem, I think in most

00:13:11.823 --> 00:13:15.013
of academics, main barrier

00:13:15.013 --> 00:13:16.583
to actually learning the academic material

00:13:16.583 --> 00:13:17.863
is just engagement.

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:21.343
And I think students at different
ages, at different stages

00:13:21.343 --> 00:13:22.753
in their academic development disengage

00:13:22.753 --> 00:13:25.893
for different reasons,
I fundamentally believe,

00:13:25.893 --> 00:13:27.633
and we've seen this, I've
seen this anecdotally

00:13:27.633 --> 00:13:29.133
at Khan Academy, we've even
seen a little bit of data

00:13:29.133 --> 00:13:33.683
that kids disengage when
they feel like the content

00:13:33.683 --> 00:13:36.473
is not for them, when
they feel like the content

00:13:36.473 --> 00:13:39.753
is either not applicable to
their life, they feel like

00:13:39.753 --> 00:13:41.423
it's too easy for them and they're bored,

00:13:41.423 --> 00:13:43.683
or they feel like it's too hard for them.

00:13:43.683 --> 00:13:46.633
And so I think a lot of what
we try to do at Khan Academy

00:13:46.633 --> 00:13:50.003
is first of all, offer content
that can be personalized

00:13:50.003 --> 00:13:51.783
to where the student is.

00:13:51.783 --> 00:13:55.313
So what I would do is, I don't
know how old your eldest son

00:13:55.313 --> 00:13:58.633
is, but have them, if they say
they're entering sixth grade,

00:13:58.633 --> 00:14:01.613
have them take the course
challenge on Khan Academy

00:14:01.613 --> 00:14:03.753
for the getting ready
for sixth grade course.

00:14:03.753 --> 00:14:05.753
And that getting ready for,
that way you'll be able

00:14:05.753 --> 00:14:07.323
to, you and your son will
be able to understand

00:14:07.323 --> 00:14:09.263
how ready they are for sixth grade,

00:14:09.263 --> 00:14:13.163
and if they aren't they
can fill in those gaps

00:14:13.163 --> 00:14:16.483
over time, and then uh they
can work at their own time

00:14:16.483 --> 00:14:17.653
and pace at the sixth grade.

00:14:17.653 --> 00:14:20.813
And to motivate them, I would remind them,

00:14:20.813 --> 00:14:23.053
you could hopefully they're
watching, you can remind them

00:14:23.053 --> 00:14:24.833
that this is really interesting stuff

00:14:24.833 --> 00:14:28.923
that's going to be really
valuable for their entire life.

00:14:28.923 --> 00:14:31.493
But what I've seen is as people
get their legs under them

00:14:31.493 --> 00:14:33.463
and they start to master the concepts,

00:14:33.463 --> 00:14:36.263
they actually really start
enjoying the learning process.

00:14:36.263 --> 00:14:40.143
I'd also recommend making
it a point of interaction

00:14:40.143 --> 00:14:42.163
between you and your child.

00:14:42.163 --> 00:14:44.143
Maybe you're doing your
work from home now,

00:14:44.143 --> 00:14:45.693
do it right next to
them, so they say, hey,

00:14:45.693 --> 00:14:46.953
let's work together for 20 minutes

00:14:46.953 --> 00:14:48.423
and then we're gonna take
a 10-minute break together,

00:14:48.423 --> 00:14:49.973
let's work together for 30 minutes,

00:14:49.973 --> 00:14:51.813
then we're gonna take a
10-minute break together.

00:14:51.813 --> 00:14:54.003
I think that might make it a lot more fun

00:14:54.003 --> 00:14:56.063
for your child, or they
could do that with some

00:14:56.063 --> 00:14:58.243
of their friends to
kind of keep them going,

00:14:58.243 --> 00:14:59.593
to have some positive peer pressure,

00:14:59.593 --> 00:15:00.543
so those are my thoughts.

00:15:00.543 --> 00:15:03.213
On the Sophie, Dan any
ideas on if a parent

00:15:03.213 --> 00:15:05.403
has a particularly, a child that seems

00:15:05.403 --> 00:15:07.533
to be a little disengaged?

00:15:07.533 --> 00:15:09.293
- Yeah, so I would echo
a lot of the things

00:15:09.293 --> 00:15:11.043
that you already mentioned,
so in our article

00:15:11.043 --> 00:15:14.893
on how to motivate,
Kristine's article on that.

00:15:14.893 --> 00:15:17.373
I think the two things
she called out is one,

00:15:17.373 --> 00:15:19.303
people are more likely to
do something if they think

00:15:19.303 --> 00:15:20.363
they're successful at it.

00:15:20.363 --> 00:15:22.723
And then number two, they're
more likely also to do

00:15:22.723 --> 00:15:24.413
if they value that activity.

00:15:24.413 --> 00:15:26.463
So in our motivation article,

00:15:26.463 --> 00:15:28.393
there's a couple recommendations,
first, is to make sure

00:15:28.393 --> 00:15:30.603
that you talk to your
child about the goals

00:15:30.603 --> 00:15:32.973
and making sure that
there's a shared goal.

00:15:32.973 --> 00:15:35.553
Number two, is just
making sure that the child

00:15:35.553 --> 00:15:36.853
is actually working towards this goal,

00:15:36.853 --> 00:15:38.403
so to monitoring progress.

00:15:38.403 --> 00:15:41.280
And I think most importantly
is also to make sure

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:45.533
that you talk to the child
about how those goals relate

00:15:45.533 --> 00:15:46.473
to their values.

00:15:46.473 --> 00:15:48.673
So is it a passion that
they're interested in,

00:15:48.673 --> 00:15:51.643
or what do they get out of
it in the long term as well.

00:15:51.643 --> 00:15:53.503
So I think those are the important things.

00:15:53.503 --> 00:15:55.393
And then also if they
get stuck at something,

00:15:55.393 --> 00:15:58.113
so this speaks to being
successful, if they get stuck

00:15:58.113 --> 00:16:00.403
with something that you have a process

00:16:00.403 --> 00:16:03.056
to help them get out of, to be unblocked.

00:16:04.323 --> 00:16:07.236
- Yeah, Sophie for the younger kids?

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:10.573
- Yeah, for younger kids
one thing that we've seen

00:16:10.573 --> 00:16:13.683
that's really worked and
you touched on this Sal

00:16:13.683 --> 00:16:16.773
