00:17:18.773 --> 00:17:22.193
you're entering let's say seventh grade.

00:17:22.193 --> 00:17:25.693
What I would recommend is
we have in math something

00:17:25.693 --> 00:17:27.863
called a get ready for
seventh grade course.

00:17:27.863 --> 00:17:29.933
And what you can do is go to that course,

00:17:29.933 --> 00:17:31.063
and it'll actually prompt you to take

00:17:31.063 --> 00:17:33.323
what's called a Course
Challenge, which samples

00:17:33.323 --> 00:17:36.003
from the entire course
for the get-ready-for.

00:17:36.003 --> 00:17:38.833
So this is all the foundational
skills for seventh grade.

00:17:38.833 --> 00:17:42.043
If you do well on that,
say, you get an 80 or 90%,

00:17:42.043 --> 00:17:44.503
that means that you're
ready for seventh grade,

00:17:44.503 --> 00:17:46.873
and so then you can start
working at your own time and pace

00:17:46.873 --> 00:17:48.443
on the seventh grade course.

00:17:48.443 --> 00:17:52.083
If you aren't doing well on
that initial course challenge,

00:17:52.083 --> 00:17:54.463
if you're getting a 50% to 60% on it,

00:17:54.463 --> 00:17:57.123
or even lower, that means
that you have some gaps

00:17:57.123 --> 00:18:00.253
in your knowledge uh that
are prerequisite skills

00:18:00.253 --> 00:18:01.703
for seventh grade.

00:18:01.703 --> 00:18:04.693
And then you can use that
get-ready-for seventh grade course

00:18:04.693 --> 00:18:07.223
to go focus on the units that
you're having trouble with,

00:18:07.223 --> 00:18:09.473
and then get mastery in
those skills, so that you can

00:18:09.473 --> 00:18:11.223
have a strong foundation, and then you

00:18:11.223 --> 00:18:13.883
can feel confident going
into seventh grade.

00:18:13.883 --> 00:18:16.173
If you're already starting
seventh grade, there's two ways

00:18:16.173 --> 00:18:18.083
to do it, you can front
load with the get-ready

00:18:18.083 --> 00:18:20.213
for grade level course
like I just talked about,

00:18:20.213 --> 00:18:21.893
or you could do it in parallel to,

00:18:21.893 --> 00:18:23.873
while you're doing your
seventh grade course

00:18:23.873 --> 00:18:25.263
at your own time and pace.

00:18:25.263 --> 00:18:28.543
So I would say, generally
speaking, if you're student

00:18:28.543 --> 00:18:30.818
or if you're the parent of a student,

00:18:30.818 --> 00:18:33.763
the system, the school
system has some grade

00:18:33.763 --> 00:18:37.963
that the the child is entering
or that you are entering,

00:18:37.963 --> 00:18:40.233
but we know that everyone
has different gaps

00:18:40.233 --> 00:18:41.593
in their knowledge, they
have different levels

00:18:41.593 --> 00:18:43.553
of preparedness, and so
that's why we created

00:18:43.553 --> 00:18:45.433
these get-ready-for grade level courses,

00:18:45.433 --> 00:18:47.083
so that you have an opportunity to fill in

00:18:47.083 --> 00:18:49.123
all your prerequisite gaps that you need,

00:18:49.123 --> 00:18:51.393
so that you have a strong
foundation for your grade level.

00:18:51.393 --> 00:18:54.423
And clearly if you find, if
you're ready for seventh grade

00:18:54.423 --> 00:18:56.633
and maybe even you know a lot
of the seventh grade material

00:18:56.633 --> 00:18:58.223
you could take the course challenge there,

00:18:58.223 --> 00:18:59.893
we have a bunch of acceleration mechanics,

00:18:59.893 --> 00:19:02.373
course challenges, unit
tests, mastery challenges

00:19:02.373 --> 00:19:04.013
so you can move through
that quickly if you know

00:19:04.013 --> 00:19:06.693
that material, and you can
imagine some seventh graders

00:19:06.693 --> 00:19:09.533
might be even ready for eighth
or even ninth grade material.

00:19:09.533 --> 00:19:13.083
So everything we do here at
Khan Academy is to help you find

00:19:13.083 --> 00:19:16.073
your learning edge, but
I would definitely start

00:19:16.073 --> 00:19:18.673
with whatever grade level
you're entering in math,

00:19:18.673 --> 00:19:20.443
and we have these get
ready grade level courses

00:19:20.443 --> 00:19:21.583
