Praveen Pal, my daughter is
three and a half years old,

00:33:27.643 --> 00:33:29.753
will be taking nursery class, can we start

00:33:29.753 --> 00:33:31.623
with your course material?

00:33:31.623 --> 00:33:33.773
And I think Sophie might
have had to drop off,

00:33:33.773 --> 00:33:35.703
I can take a first stab at this,

00:33:35.703 --> 00:33:37.903
simple interest, oh,
Sophie's there even better.

00:33:37.903 --> 00:33:41.943
So Sophie Praveen's daughter
is three and a half years old,

00:33:41.943 --> 00:33:44.393
can we start her on Khan Academy Kids,

00:33:44.393 --> 00:33:46.913
and how would you recommend doing that?

00:33:46.913 --> 00:33:50.993
- Yeah, so Sal absolutely,
I think starting

00:33:50.993 --> 00:33:53.493
on Khan Academy Kids with
a three and a half year old

00:33:53.493 --> 00:33:56.283
is a great plan, so the
logistics side of it,

00:33:56.283 --> 00:33:58.903
you download our app from your app store,

00:33:58.903 --> 00:34:01.203
and you can quickly set up an account

00:34:01.203 --> 00:34:03.773
and add your child's profile there.

00:34:03.773 --> 00:34:07.673
And then what I would
recommend is there's actually

00:34:07.673 --> 00:34:10.113
a big play button in
the center when you come

00:34:10.113 --> 00:34:11.493
into the home screen,

00:34:11.493 --> 00:34:13.733
and that is a personalized learning path.

00:34:13.733 --> 00:34:16.223
So if you set up your three
and a half year old, say,

00:34:16.223 --> 00:34:19.633
as an age three profile
on Khan Academy Kids.

00:34:19.633 --> 00:34:22.363
That personalized learning
path will actually serve up

00:34:22.363 --> 00:34:26.580
a mixture of reading of math
of social emotional learning,

00:34:26.580 --> 00:34:30.113
all the things your child
needs to be kindergarten ready,

00:34:30.113 --> 00:34:33.323
at their pace, and it will
adapt, it will get smart

00:34:33.323 --> 00:34:35.423
to where your child is at.

00:34:35.423 --> 00:34:38.586
And I think that's probably
a great way to start.

00:34:39.803 --> 00:34:43.663
Obviously lots of parents
differ on screen time

00:34:43.663 --> 00:34:45.863
for a child of that
age and we really defer

00:34:45.863 --> 00:34:48.503
to the American Association
of Pediatrics on that.

00:34:48.503 --> 00:34:51.573
What our research shows is that between

00:34:51.573 --> 00:34:54.513
about 15 and 25 minutes a
day depending on the age

00:34:54.513 --> 00:34:56.933
of your child, maybe
three to five times a week

00:34:56.933 --> 00:35:00.133
is where we start to really see
those learning gains pick up

00:35:01.173 --> 00:35:03.956
and enjoy I would say go for it.

